# The bound is a local that no turn stores: the least of two results of calls, a number as far as anybody knows. The turns call a function that is not copied, so a copy that counts on quiet turns is left in every turn. The loop is built twice all the same, with the calls staying in the typed copy.
# REQUIRES: entries-of-bun
# RUN: walk f3 mechanisms=all
# The bound is asked once, in front of the loop.
# CHECK: TypeTest {{*}} testedType=i32
# The loop as written: the bound is asked for its kind in every turn and the counter is an integer up to 2 ** 53.
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: Less {{*}} form=NumberAndValue
# CHECK: Increment {{*}} form=CheckedIntegers
# What is no int32 is rounded up once; what is no number goes to the loop as written.
# CHECK: IntegerBound {{*}} comparison=Less
# The typed copy: two integers are compared, both calls stand in it, and the counter is stepped as an int32.
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: Less {{*}} form=Integers
# CHECK: CallDirect {{*}} function=f2
# CHECK: CallDirect {{*}} function=f2
# CHECK: Increment {{*}} form=Integers
